// Hand-curated position characteristics (position_rules_sets) for genuine
// GAP-FILL cases only, plus the positions those entries reference.
//
// The invariant every entry in this file must satisfy: the
// (position, rules set) pair is one NO source importer can ever produce a row
// for. That is what makes curating it BEFORE the source importers run safe:
// PositionRulesSetsService.sync matches by the natural key
// (position_id, rules_set_id) and updates in place, so if an importer could
// also write that pair, its value would silently overwrite the curated one.
//
// Deciding an entry belongs here is a case-by-case judgment call every time,
// never a rule about the rules set. BBL's snapshot-assignment logic
// (BblPositionRaceErasImportService / BblPositionCharacteristicsImportService)
// can write a row under any rules set its era covers whose agilityFormat
// isn't 'bare' -- BB2020 included -- whenever it finds real scraped usage
// evidence. So "it is a BB2020 entry" is not a reason to put something here.
// CRP, CRP+ and BB2016 are a separate case: BBL never writes a row for those
// three at all, but that alone still doesn't make an entry belong HERE --
// the fully-curated after-other-importers/position-characteristics.json5
// already owns them; this file is only for a pair no importer, source or
// curated-after-phase, ever supplies. Before adding an entry, establish that
// neither BBL nor TP can produce a candidate for that position at all.
//
// Giant Mercenary is the one entry that qualifies today. BBL never creates a
// position candidate for it: a mercenary is not a scraped race-roster
// position and is not BBL-flagged as a star player. TP creates the position
// (TpPlayerPositionService's mercenary-position resolution, from a hire's
// inline fallbackPositionName) but supplies no characteristics for it
// anywhere -- the name appears in no roster catalog, and the match-embedded
// lineUps[] entry for an actual hire carries no ma/st/ag/pa/av either. So
// nothing can overwrite the row below, and TpMercenaryCharacteristicsService
// reads it back directly from position_rules_sets (via packages/game-data's
// PositionRulesSetsService, not an RPC call) to give each hire real values.
//
// BB2025 has no Giant Mercenary published yet, so it has no entry here
// either -- that absence is intentional, not a gap to fill.
//
// Note: tools/review-race's per-race characteristics panels structurally
// exclude all star players (Giant Mercenary is one), so this entry does not
// appear there regardless of which phase curates it -- a pre-existing,
// unrelated limitation of that tool, not something this file's placement
// affects. tools/review-race's own unit tests (manual-raw-data.service.spec.ts)
// verify the pooling of this file with position-characteristics.json5
// directly instead.
//
// Each `positions` entry here registers the external ids the source importers
// will send for that position, so their own upsert lands on this row rather
// than creating a second one -- the same technique star-players.json5 uses.
// For a mercenary that means TP's tourplay.net id and TP's "Name" id, both of
// which are the bare position name (NameExternalIdService.forStarPosition).
//
// Every `position` reference below is a "Name" external id. BB2020 entries
// must carry `passing`: BB2020 declares passingFormat 'plus_zero_legal', and
// the API rejects an entry that omits a Passing value for it.
//
// Sources:
//   BB2020 -- Death Zone Season 2, "Mercenaries" chapter, transcribed from
//             the developer's physical copy of that supplement, not estimated
//             from general series knowledge.
{
  externalSystems: [
    { name: 'tourplay.net', category: 'imported_data_source' },
    { name: 'Name', category: 'bookkeeping' },
  ],
  positions: [
    {
      name: 'Giant Mercenary',
      isStarPlayer: true,
      externalIds: [
        { system: 'tourplay.net', id: 'Giant Mercenary' },
        { system: 'Name', id: 'Giant Mercenary' },
      ],
    },
  ],
  positionRulesSets: [
    { position: { system: 'Name', id: 'Giant Mercenary' }, rulesSet: { system: 'Name', id: 'BB2020' }, move: 6, strength: 7, agility: 5, passing: 5, armour: 11 },
  ],
}
